From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:45:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add a host default permission mode per provider

New agents took their mode from whatever each device last remembered, so a
host owner could not make every client start agents in the same mode. The
host config now stores an optional defaultModeId per provider
(agents.providers.<id>.defaultModeId), editable through the mutable daemon
config; null clears it.

When the mode still exists in the provider's catalog, the daemon reports it
as the provider's defaultModeId (so clients with nothing remembered use it)
plus a new hostDefaultModeId snapshot field, and uses it for top-level,
attended creates that omit a mode. Parent inheritance, unattended selection
and explicit modes are unchanged, and a stale id falls back to the
provider's own default.

The app gates on the new server_info.features.providerDefaultMode flag: Host
settings > Agents gets a per-provider picker, and agent form resolution lets
a host default beat the per-device remembered mode while explicit initial
modes still win.

Fork-Change: F-3
